{
  "title": "Likes, wants, skills and feelings",
  "note": "好き, きらい, 上手, 下手 and できます mark their object with が: 猫が好きです. To want a thing is ほしいです (車がほしいです); to want to do something, add たいです to the verb stem (食べたいです). たい works like an い-adjective: 行きたくないです. 〜と思います means \"I think that...\"",
  "src": {
    "t": "Tae Kim's Guide to Learning Japanese",
    "u": "https://guidetojapanese.org/learn/grammar"
  },
